<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys Feb heavy naphtha at almost $250/tonne.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys Feb heavy naphtha at almost $250/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought by tender 28,000 tonnes of heavy naphthenic and aromatic (N+A) naphtha at almost $250 per tonne, a company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closed December 30 and was valid until December 31. It sought a cargo cost-and-freight Kaohsiung February 19-28.</p>
<p>In its last spot tender, CPC bought a 28,000-tonne cargo of similar grade naphtha at $230 per tonne for delivery November 21-30.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
